Project origin and acknowledgement
----------------------------------

DraftHarbor began as a personal fork of Writingway 2:
https://github.com/aomukai/Writingway2

The initial motivation was to improve support for newer DeepSeek models and
Chinese long-form writing workflows. Continued development replaced the web
runtime with an Electron desktop architecture, introduced new storage and
service layers, redesigned the user interface and data model, and added an
independent test and release system.

We thank the Writingway 2 author and contributors for publishing their work
and for the early product ideas around projects, scenes, compendium entries,
workshop conversations and AI-assisted writing.

Writingway 2 states in its README that it is released under the MIT License.
Copyright in Writingway 2 remains with its original author and contributors.
DraftHarbor is not an official release, translation or endorsed branch of
Writingway 2. Questions about DraftHarbor should not be directed to the
Writingway 2 maintainers.

The DraftHarbor logo and application icon are newly generated original assets
created for this project. They do not reuse the Writingway logo.

